  "image_tag": "bench-glom",
  "instruction": "## Goal\n\nWhen a user accesses a dunder attribute (e.g., `T.__name__`) on a `T` spec, the resulting `AttributeError` should include a helpful message that names the exact attribute and explains how to access it using `T.__(\"...\")`.\n\n## Observable behavior\n\n```python\ndef test_t_dunders():\n    with raises(AttributeError) as exc_info:\n        T.__name__\n\n    assert 'use T.__(\"name__\")' in str(exc_info.value)\n\n    assert glom(1, T.__('class__')) is int\n```\n\n## Constraints\n\n- Keep the existing exception type (`AttributeError`) and behavior unchanged.\n- Do not rename or remove any public API visible in the tests (e.g., `glom`, `Path`, `S`, `T`, `A`, `PathAccessError`, `GlomError`, `BadSpec`).\n- Files in scope: `glom/__init__.py`, `glom/core.py`, `glom/grouping.py`, `glom/matching.py`, `glom/mutation.py`, `glom/reduction.py`, `glom/streaming.py`, `glom/test/test_path_and_t.py`.\n\n## How success is measured\n\n```\npython -m pytest -q glom/test/test_path_and_t.py::test_t_dunders\n```",
